# Raw and derived data are never committed.
# The repository ships the code that produces the data, not the data itself.
# Anyone cloning this repo rebuilds it from source with one command.
# IPEDS files are public and stable, so re-downloading is cheap and the
# alternative, a multi-gigabyte repository, is not.
data/raw/
data/interim/
data/logs/
*.zip
*.csv
*.parquet

# Exception: small reference files that ARE part of the repository.
!config/*.csv
!docs/*.csv
!requirements.txt

# Secrets. Never commit.
.env
*.pem
*.key
credentials.json

# Personal documents. This repository is public.
# The resume and transcript contain a phone number, a home city and academic
# records. None of that belongs on the internet.
*.pdf
Celsia_Arockiadass_Master_Resume_Updated.pdf
MS-DA-Unofficial Transcript.pdf

# Private working memory, deliberately excluded from the public repository.
# BUILD_PLAN.md and PROGRESS.md reference the job search: named employers,
# rejections, and the gap analysis behind this project. They are the reason
# the project exists and they are excellent working documents, but they are
# not for public consumption. The repository carries README.md and the docs/
# folder instead, written for a hiring institutional research director.
BUILD_PLAN.md
PROGRESS.md

# Python
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# R
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/

# Power BI temporary files. The .pbix itself IS committed.
*.pbix.tmp
~$*

# SQL Server local artifacts
*.mdf
*.ldf
*.bak

# Editors and OS
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.swp

# Windows shortcut and lock files
*.lnk
